From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:31:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: start passthrough on the frame grid before video
 moves

A passthrough start sync pads its error with a pause shorter than a
frame, which stops the stream on the wire. Silent frames pad only whole
frames, so the clock must take the rest before the picture moves.
Audio-only resyncs of a stamped stream (offset change, track switch
without a seek, steady-play error over 100 ms) start the same way.
